  "id": "tbilisi_kalakuri",
  "name": "Kalakuri simghera (Tbilisi city song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The European-oriented strand of Tbilisi's urban song, which took shape in the nineteenth and early twentieth centuries as Georgian singers combined their own part-singing with the harmony of Russian and European romance. Sung by small ensembles in three-part harmony or by soloists with guitar, it was widely recorded by Melodiya and stands beside the Eastern-oriented sazandari repertoire as one of the two strands of Georgian city music.",
  "recipe": "classic early-1940s kalakuri simghera, ballad Poetry. parallel thirds two voice. classical nylon-string guitar, a cappella small 3 to 8 one per part global traditional polyphonic choir ensemble. treated studio. Neumann U47, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, Telefunken u73b broadcast comp. tape 15ips hall reverb.",
